## A. nearest-rank percentile helper off by one (benchmarks/r177/sse_fanout_bench.py, tool_families_bench.py, benchmarks/sec10/ready_perf.py)
cause: k = int(round(p/100*n + 0.5)) - 1 — Python's round() is banker's rounding, so when p/100*n is an integer the result
rounds to EVEN: sometimes the correct rank, sometimes one above. Correct nearest-rank = ceil(p/100*n) (same as scripts/r177_stop_limits.nearest_rank).
### RED (tests/test_r177_local_gap_benches.py::test_nearest_rank_percentile_is_exact_in_every_bench_tool + ::test_sse_bench_percentile_and_loopback_helpers, before the fix)
