## B. CI-only flaky assertion in tests/test_r177_per_service.py::test_real_baseline_health
NOTE: found and fixed during this batch; the fix itself was MERGED WITH PR #332 (D-135 addendum, log 376) because it blocked that PR's CI.
The red/green below was recorded on this branch before the move; log 376 carries the authoritative red/green for the merged fix.
CI run 42379128155 (PR #332, attempt 1): `assert abs(raw nearest-rank p95 - k6 summary p95) < 0.01` → 0.0531 (4.106 vs 4.0529ms).
cause: k6 Trend p(q) interpolates linearly at position q*(n-1); the runner reports nearest-rank. Two different definitions; they agree
within 0.01ms only when neighbouring samples are close — a contract that never existed. Not related to SEC-10 (volatile CI, /health baseline).
fix: scripts/r177_stop_limits.k6_trend_quantile (k6's formula) + raw_quantiles.p95_ms_k6_method in the runner; the test now compares like with like
(k6 method vs k6 summary < 0.01ms). Reports still declare nearest-rank. No threshold relaxed.
